@* S-24: Account → My access. What the signed-in user's roles let them do in CaseBook, and how access changes, so
   nobody has to discover their limits by hitting them. *@
@page "/account/access"
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>My access</PageTitle>

<PageHeader Title="My access"
            Subtitle="What your CaseBook roles let you do. Roles come from your Active Directory groups." />

<div class="im-card p-3 mb-3" style="max-width: 48rem">
    <AccessSummary Detailed="true" />
</div>

<div class="small text-muted" style="max-width: 48rem">
    <p class="mb-1"><strong>Restricted cases.</strong> A case restricted to need-to-know is visible only to its incident commander,
        the people assigned to it, and roles with <em>View restricted</em> or <em>View all cases</em>.</p>
    <p class="mb-0"><strong>Changing your access.</strong> Ask a CaseBook administrator. Changes to a role or its AD group mapping
        reach you within a few minutes. Membership of a new AD group takes effect the next time you sign in to Windows.</p>
</div>
